WEBVTT

01:54.114 --> 01:56.116
Okay, thanks for your patience.

02:01.830 --> 02:02.747
We're through.

02:05.917 --> 02:07.377
Didn't mean to meddle.

02:09.129 --> 02:14.342
But after you battled the strongest man
in the history of Earth,

02:15.135 --> 02:17.053
these tests at least seemed necessary.

02:17.846 --> 02:21.057
Actually, considering
the kind of life you've led,

02:21.808 --> 02:24.185
I'd even say these tests came very late.

02:27.147 --> 02:29.232
Even pro martial arts fighters

02:29.315 --> 02:32.152
don't have as much damage
done to their bodies as yours.

02:33.153 --> 02:36.156
I've known this kind of thing
was necessary,

02:36.823 --> 02:41.369
but it's not like I can change my way
of life even if we find something wrong.

02:42.871 --> 02:45.081
Yes, I realize that too.

02:46.082 --> 02:49.252
You can assume there's nothing wrong
if I don't contact you.

02:49.335 --> 02:50.587
Thank you.

03:01.764 --> 03:02.849
It's me.

03:02.932 --> 03:05.018
Get over here, now!

03:07.520 --> 03:09.105
That's right. Right now!

03:10.190 --> 03:13.359
There are 60 million other women
out there. Get over here now!

03:19.199 --> 03:20.658
This is unbelievable...

03:25.705 --> 03:27.248
Yeah, Kureha?

03:27.916 --> 03:29.792
Mogi, get over here.

03:30.335 --> 03:33.755
For you, there may be
60 million women out there.

03:33.838 --> 03:37.550
But in my life, I'll be lucky
if I meet even six of them.

03:37.634 --> 03:39.093
Mogi, look at this.

03:42.680 --> 03:43.514
What?

03:44.224 --> 03:47.518
What?! Is that a brain?!

03:48.853 --> 03:51.189
A genuine hominid.

03:51.272 --> 03:54.275
It's the frontal lobe
of a Japanese male, age 18.

03:54.359 --> 03:59.405
These creases, or folds, they're...

03:59.489 --> 04:00.990
No way!

04:01.866 --> 04:04.786
Neuroscientist Kenjiro Mogi,

04:05.662 --> 04:09.123
I'd like to ask your opinion
as the country's best expert in the field.

04:09.624 --> 04:13.336
Though I am not as great as you are,
I am still a neuroscientist.

04:14.087 --> 04:17.757
The shape of the folds of the brain
are not related to character.

04:17.840 --> 04:19.300
That's an absolute given.

04:19.384 --> 04:23.221
However, even without comparing this
to an ordinary brain,

04:24.013 --> 04:25.974
it's clear this one is demonic.

04:27.267 --> 04:28.268
So, Mogi.

04:29.352 --> 04:32.939
The folds of the brain
and character are not related, right?

04:35.817 --> 04:36.693
Kureha...

04:36.776 --> 04:37.610
Yeah?

04:37.694 --> 04:43.408
We really don't know anything
about the brain, do we?

04:44.284 --> 04:46.869
The brain is incredible.

04:46.953 --> 04:48.705
The brain is awesome!

04:49.414 --> 04:52.583
Whether this is a product of chance
or a trick played by God,

04:52.667 --> 04:55.712
it's incredible
we've come across this miracle!

04:56.671 --> 05:00.008
As to your question...

05:00.550 --> 05:04.012
Yes, well...

05:04.095 --> 05:07.682
I have to speak responsibly
as a neuroscientist.

05:07.765 --> 05:09.475
The folds of the brain and character?

05:09.559 --> 05:10.810
Don't disappoint me.

05:13.354 --> 05:15.773
Kureha, in this case,

05:16.441 --> 05:18.526
the character of this person...

05:19.819 --> 05:22.989
It's clearly obvious he's like a demon!

05:25.116 --> 05:25.992
Mogi...

05:27.327 --> 05:29.162
You're right about that.

05:29.245 --> 05:31.998
I mean,
I really can't explain it, you know.

05:35.126 --> 05:38.504
<i>On this day in a certain park in Tokyo...</i>

05:45.595 --> 05:48.222
<i>There was a short article
about a massive surge of rats</i>

05:48.306 --> 05:50.933
<i>in the morning newspapers the next day.</i>

05:52.352 --> 05:54.604
<i>However, not a single person knew</i>

05:55.146 --> 06:00.193
<i>that the cause of this surge was a lone
young man who passed through the area</i>

06:00.860 --> 06:02.487
<i>immediately after the surge.</i>

06:11.037 --> 06:12.038
<i>Astonishing...</i>

06:14.082 --> 06:15.875
<i>That was an astonishing face.</i>

06:19.003 --> 06:21.381
<i>That handsome face,
filled with the confidence</i>

06:22.006 --> 06:23.883
<i>that he could get anything he wanted.</i>

06:24.467 --> 06:26.719
<i>From that face that believed in his future</i>

06:28.388 --> 06:30.306
<i>to when everything had crumbled away.</i>

06:31.140 --> 06:36.938
<i>Pretense, arrogance, false courage,
self-importance, pride, and ego.</i>

06:37.522 --> 06:38.648
<i>His tears,</i>

06:39.273 --> 06:40.400
<i>snot,</i>

06:41.025 --> 06:42.151
<i>and saliva...</i>

06:42.777 --> 06:46.364
<i>The fluid that consisted
of all those mixed together,</i>

06:47.782 --> 06:48.950
<i>it was beautiful.</i>

06:52.078 --> 06:54.664
<i>That wasn't wrong of me.</i>

07:00.044 --> 07:02.755
<i>I wonder how long we were like that.</i>

07:05.299 --> 07:09.846
<i>Around the time my clothes
became heavy with his tears...</i>

07:17.895 --> 07:22.733
From the depths of my heart,
I am grateful for what you have done.

07:30.575 --> 07:32.577
Can I ask you one thing?

07:32.660 --> 07:33.494
Huh?

07:33.578 --> 07:38.124
Why did you hold me for so long?

07:38.624 --> 07:43.546
You did it so kindly, so full of heart,
and with such passion.

07:45.673 --> 07:47.550
I can't really explain it well,

07:48.092 --> 07:52.096
but if it were your mother,
surely she would have done the same.

07:52.597 --> 07:56.058
But I'm not even your boyfriend.

07:56.601 --> 07:58.019
I did it out of love.

07:58.603 --> 08:02.106
Huh? I don't understand what you mean.

08:02.190 --> 08:04.525
Why love someone who's not your boyfriend?

08:05.276 --> 08:08.279
There's no need for romance
in acts of love.

08:09.864 --> 08:14.535
Your mother didn't need to be
in love with you to love you.

08:16.579 --> 08:19.916
It seems I fell in love
with an incredible woman.

08:19.999 --> 08:23.544
Compared to you,
I'm still a novice in love.

08:25.379 --> 08:29.509
I bet the person who showed you that love

08:29.592 --> 08:31.636
was Baki Hanma, right?

08:33.679 --> 08:34.972
<i>I lost the fight...</i>

08:36.849 --> 08:38.267
<i>and lost my love.</i>

08:39.894 --> 08:43.272
Thank you again for this wonderful love.

08:45.274 --> 08:47.860
<i>Did she break my heart? Don't be stupid.</i>

08:48.528 --> 08:52.365
<i>Baki Hanma didn't even
have to compete for it.</i>

08:54.492 --> 08:55.368
<i>In love,</i>

08:57.161 --> 08:59.080
<i>I couldn't even become a loser.</i>

09:08.589 --> 09:09.674
See you later.

09:19.809 --> 09:22.270
Sometimes we go forever
without seeing each other.

09:24.313 --> 09:26.899
Aren't you going to ask what I was up to?

09:28.150 --> 09:29.193
What were you up to?

09:30.820 --> 09:32.113
I was being happy.

09:33.656 --> 09:35.241
That's what I figured.

09:38.828 --> 09:40.580
You know I was kidding!

09:42.373 --> 09:47.003
<i>As long as you're happy,
then it doesn't have to be with me.</i>

09:48.379 --> 09:50.840
<i>I'm not detached enough to think that.</i>

09:52.049 --> 09:52.883
<i>Not yet.</i>

09:54.260 --> 09:56.929
<i>I'd still like us
to be together a little longer.</i>

10:03.060 --> 10:05.855
You want another taste? Do ya?

10:08.357 --> 10:09.900
Now hand over your wallet.

10:10.401 --> 10:11.527
Kure-chan.

10:12.653 --> 10:14.030
Why don't you slice him up?

10:17.867 --> 10:19.035
Good idea.

10:25.875 --> 10:27.627
<i>To thugs like them,</i>

10:27.710 --> 10:30.796
<i>proper analysis of their prey's power
is a matter of life and death.</i>

10:31.631 --> 10:35.384
<i>Later, the young man spoke
of this situation like this,</i>

10:36.427 --> 10:38.429
<i>"The knife that was in my hand...</i>

10:40.556 --> 10:41.849
<i>it shrunk."</i>

10:43.100 --> 10:48.272
<i>"It transformed into something so small
and useless, like a keychain."</i>

10:49.774 --> 10:50.733
Now, son...

10:54.612 --> 10:57.323
You really shouldn't pick on the weak.

10:58.908 --> 11:00.326
Mr. Kuriyagawa.

11:01.494 --> 11:04.205
You boys, you should thank me.

11:04.747 --> 11:08.084
If I'd spoken to you even a second later,

11:08.167 --> 11:11.545
you could have suffered
broken facial bones, brain contusions,

11:11.629 --> 11:15.424
ruptured organs,
fractured teeth, or blindness.

11:16.300 --> 11:19.595
In any case, you would have been
a horrible sight to see.

11:22.807 --> 11:23.641
Get out of here.

11:28.521 --> 11:29.689
It's been a while.

11:30.981 --> 11:32.233
You're looking well.

11:38.030 --> 11:39.156
It won't be long now.

11:40.533 --> 11:43.953
The greatest on Earth,
the most powerful in history,

11:44.036 --> 11:46.372
the greatest and final fight
between father and son.

11:53.003 --> 11:56.132
It's just a simple fight
between father and son.

12:02.304 --> 12:04.140
Vengeance for your mother.

12:04.765 --> 12:06.559
The time for that is now.

12:07.601 --> 12:08.644
Mr. Kuriyagawa...

12:10.896 --> 12:12.523
It's been five years since then.

12:20.364 --> 12:21.240
Baki...

12:21.866 --> 12:24.535
Make your father happy!

12:26.120 --> 12:27.621
Dad!

12:34.628 --> 12:35.546
Many times...

12:37.214 --> 12:38.549
Many, many, many times...

12:39.508 --> 12:41.844
Many times I have questioned myself.

12:44.013 --> 12:45.431
My father whom I despise...

12:47.391 --> 12:49.685
Do I actually hate him?

12:50.936 --> 12:53.189
To put it another way, Mr. Kuriyagawa,

12:53.856 --> 12:55.858
is it true that my father, Yujiro Hanma,

12:56.442 --> 13:00.404
deserves my vengeance for the death
of my mother, Emi Akezawa?

13:04.158 --> 13:05.826
What makes you ask that?

13:07.453 --> 13:10.956
My mother was no ordinary mother.

13:16.962 --> 13:18.172
<i>Emi Akezawa.</i>

13:19.381 --> 13:21.967
<i>By marrying Eiichi Akezawa,</i>

13:22.468 --> 13:25.137
<i>head of one of the world's
supremely wealthy families</i>,

13:25.221 --> 13:28.098
<i>she had been promised
a life of magnificence.</i>

13:40.486 --> 13:41.320
<i>However...</i>

13:43.489 --> 13:45.825
<i>she met the strongest man in the world.</i>

13:48.911 --> 13:50.996
<i>And that changed everything.</i>

13:56.710 --> 14:00.756
<i>Seeing a person injured,
crushed and killed.</i>

14:01.882 --> 14:05.094
<i>She desired more than anyone else
to see those things.</i>

14:06.387 --> 14:09.265
<i>The cruelty that was hidden within her,</i>

14:10.099 --> 14:13.018
<i>Yujiro perceived it in her from the start.</i>

14:22.486 --> 14:23.654
Where's the woman?

14:24.822 --> 14:26.490
I knew at first sight.

14:26.574 --> 14:29.952
More than anyone and anything else,
you like to see blood.

14:31.745 --> 14:33.998
Look at your face in a mirror.

14:36.083 --> 14:37.209
You're smiling.

14:39.628 --> 14:41.630
You're the woman I've been looking for.

14:43.257 --> 14:45.759
Give birth to my child.

14:49.972 --> 14:52.182
<i>She wasn't an ordinary mother.</i>

14:54.226 --> 14:56.562
<i>As the one in charge of Baki's education,</i>

14:57.146 --> 15:00.065
<i>she gave him a place to live
and money for living expenses.</i>

15:00.983 --> 15:05.446
<i>She also provided a top-level coach
and top-level facilities.</i>

15:06.155 --> 15:09.617
<i>She raised Baki
to become an elite fighter.</i>

15:12.786 --> 15:15.372
<i>She did it all
for the greatest man of all men...</i>

15:15.456 --> 15:17.291
<i>No, the ultimate male.</i>

15:17.833 --> 15:20.169
<i>To gain the love of Yujiro Hanma.</i>

15:21.378 --> 15:22.713
Just one more week.

15:23.714 --> 15:28.844
Then I can give him my present,
Baki, the greatest present of all.

15:30.095 --> 15:32.848
<i>She couldn't care less about her son,
who shared her blood.</i>

15:33.599 --> 15:37.061
<i>This woman chose to be a martyr
for romantic love over maternal love.</i>

15:37.144 --> 15:40.230
<i>Baki was nothing more
than a tool to achieve that end.</i>

15:42.775 --> 15:46.153
<i>However, the only thing that Yujiro wanted</i>

15:46.946 --> 15:51.241
<i>was a strong Baki who would fight him,
nothing else.</i>

15:52.701 --> 15:55.537
<i>You're merely responsible
for raising Baki.</i>

15:58.999 --> 16:03.629
If, in his next fight,
Baki doesn't perform to my satisfaction,

16:04.213 --> 16:08.884
then you're no more than
just a worthless middle-aged prostitute.

16:09.718 --> 16:12.137
Consider our relationship non-existent.

16:14.473 --> 16:16.433
<i>She wanted love.</i>

16:18.894 --> 16:23.273
Why? Why won't he love me?

16:23.357 --> 16:25.025
Because you're weak!

16:25.109 --> 16:28.070
You're weak! It's because you're weak!

16:28.612 --> 16:30.280
You're weak!

16:30.364 --> 16:36.120
Why the hell did I have
a weak child like you?!

16:38.998 --> 16:39.832
Mom,

16:41.417 --> 16:43.168
I want you to answer my question.

16:44.044 --> 16:47.047
If I defeat Yujiro,

16:48.924 --> 16:51.552
will you love me?

16:55.139 --> 16:57.099
<i>He also wanted love.</i>

17:01.270 --> 17:03.147
Between dream and reality...

17:05.357 --> 17:07.151
<i>I witnessed that scene.</i>

17:08.777 --> 17:12.406
<i>My mother being embraced
by my father, Yujiro.</i>

17:14.366 --> 17:16.952
<i>You're embracing her too damn hard, Dad.</i>

17:18.954 --> 17:20.789
<i>Mom embraced him too.</i>

17:22.750 --> 17:23.792
<i>And she cried.</i>

17:29.923 --> 17:31.341
Those tears,

17:32.551 --> 17:34.344
I wonder what they were for.

17:35.679 --> 17:37.848
Oh, stop kidding with me.

17:37.931 --> 17:39.975
Kid with you?

17:40.934 --> 17:42.644
Obviously, she felt requited.

17:44.688 --> 17:47.107
My mother's deepest desires as a woman

17:48.108 --> 17:50.110
were fulfilled in that instant.

17:53.280 --> 17:57.785
Baki, do you find that acceptable?

18:03.457 --> 18:06.877
Your mother was fulfilled as a woman.

18:07.544 --> 18:08.962
That is quite true.

18:11.465 --> 18:14.259
But it was only your mother's life
that was fulfilled.

18:14.927 --> 18:16.470
Not your life, Baki.

18:19.348 --> 18:22.101
What's important is your own life.

18:22.184 --> 18:24.645
It should be your own life
that's important.

18:25.813 --> 18:26.730
I know that.

18:29.608 --> 18:31.193
I wonder if you do.

18:31.276 --> 18:33.153
It doesn't seem that way to me.

18:33.946 --> 18:35.989
You really are worried about me.

18:36.532 --> 18:39.409
No. I am scolding you.

18:40.244 --> 18:42.788
You only have one life to live, Baki.

18:43.497 --> 18:45.165
You should not take it lightly.

18:47.751 --> 18:50.087
Living to satisfy your mother.

18:50.170 --> 18:52.506
Living to satisfy Mister Yujiro.

18:53.132 --> 18:55.926
Your mother might praise you,
that you've done well.

18:56.009 --> 19:00.180
Mr. Yujiro might praise you
and say you have "Hanma blood."

19:00.764 --> 19:02.432
But this is wrong.

19:04.560 --> 19:05.686
Baki,

19:06.395 --> 19:09.314
where do you want your life to go?

19:19.283 --> 19:20.450
I heard it.

19:20.534 --> 19:22.202
You heard?

19:23.078 --> 19:26.373
It was the words of an angel.

19:30.127 --> 19:32.212
<i>The straight punch my father hit me with,</i>

19:32.713 --> 19:34.840
<i>I felt how far I was
from measuring up to him.</i>

19:36.842 --> 19:38.093
<i>That's when it happened.</i>

19:39.011 --> 19:42.306
<i>Mom stood up in front
of the strongest man in the world.</i>

19:43.348 --> 19:44.266
Yujiro!

19:46.393 --> 19:49.771
<i>Not only that, but my mother
also punched that great brute,</i>

19:50.856 --> 19:54.610
<i>and with her chest puffed out,
she proudly said...</i>

19:55.861 --> 19:57.821
You're fighting me now!

20:02.159 --> 20:06.914
I think you understand what it means
to stand face-to-face with Yujiro Hanma.

20:07.748 --> 20:12.419
I think you understand what it means
to touch the body of Yujiro Hanma.

20:13.253 --> 20:18.425
I think you understand what it means
to challenge Yujiro to a fight.

20:23.096 --> 20:26.850
She tried to save me with her own life.

20:32.648 --> 20:34.191
That was enough for me.

20:35.234 --> 20:37.945
Those words were enough.

20:39.780 --> 20:42.032
I could even trade what remains of my life

20:43.408 --> 20:44.701
for those words.

20:46.036 --> 20:47.537
Because of what she said,

20:48.747 --> 20:49.915
I've been able to live.

20:51.416 --> 20:55.212
Because of what she said,
I've been able to be strong.

20:56.213 --> 20:59.258
All the strength that is within me,

21:00.008 --> 21:01.468
the source of it is

21:02.427 --> 21:03.804
those words.

21:06.807 --> 21:07.683
And

21:09.184 --> 21:10.602
because of those words,

21:11.395 --> 21:15.983
you are now trying to become
the strongest in the world.

21:26.285 --> 21:28.996
Don't get carried away, Kuriyagawa.

21:31.206 --> 21:35.335
Having heard the words she said,
I feel terribly ashamed.

21:36.044 --> 21:39.965
The one who was wrong was me, Kuriyagawa.

21:40.590 --> 21:41.550
No...

21:48.056 --> 21:50.642
<i>The feeling in his heart
couldn't be put into words.</i>

21:51.143 --> 21:54.062
<i>He began to realize what it was
as he put it into action.</i>

21:55.814 --> 21:57.524
<i>With Kuriyagawa before him,</i>

21:58.483 --> 22:02.529
<i>he began to realize it
while speaking about things from the past.</i>

22:04.323 --> 22:06.033
<i>His desire to surpass his father,</i>

22:07.159 --> 22:09.161
<i>his destiny to defeat his father,</i>

22:10.704 --> 22:13.790
<i>they were his response
to his mother's kindness.</i>

22:15.375 --> 22:17.169
<i>It wasn't for vengeance.</i>
